    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Patient-reported oral symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports hard yellow material along the gums that does not come off when brushing; yellow/brown build-up, especially on the lower front teeth, present for at least a few months and worsening over the last 2–3 months. Reports puffy gums that bleed when brushing, but not otherwise. No pain, ulcers, toothache, facial swelling, or trouble eating. Partner has sometimes commented on bad breath."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Oral examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Quick, limited examination with torch: generalised soft plaque and obvious supragingival calculus along gingival margins, especially lingual lower incisors and buccal upper molars. Gums erythematous and mildly swollen, with slight bleeding on gentle probing. No obvious caries, broken teeth, or mobility on finger pressure. No pus, abscess, sinus, or trismus. Tongue, buccal mucosa, and palate normal; no thrush."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
